1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,642
Mirage.

2
00:00:01,592 --> 00:00:07,881
Kubernetes-native preview environments that appear for a pull request — and vanish when you're done.

3
00:00:07,881 --> 00:00:11,026
Every PR deserves a real environment.

4
00:00:11,026 --> 00:00:13,710
Not a shared staging cluster.

5
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:16,236
Not YAML archaeology.

6
00:00:16,236 --> 00:00:23,723
With PreviewTemplate, platform teams set the defaults: resources, networking, ingress, TTL.

7
00:00:23,723 --> 00:00:28,210
Developers only specify what changes for their pull request.

8
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:30,789
Apply a PreviewEnvironment.

9
00:00:30,789 --> 00:00:32,907
Watch it come alive —

10
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:34,842
NamespaceReady.

11
00:00:34,842 --> 00:00:36,671
WorkloadReady.

12
00:00:36,671 --> 00:00:38,513
NetworkReady.

13
00:00:38,513 --> 00:00:40,144
RouteReady.

14
00:00:40,144 --> 00:00:41,894
One click.

15
00:00:41,894 --> 00:00:45,000
A live URL that matches the PR.

16
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,618
Need more than a single container?

17
00:00:47,618 --> 00:00:52,473
Declare multiple services — API, frontend, worker —

18
00:00:52,473 --> 00:00:57,934
each with its own deployment, and optional dependencies like Postgres and Redis,

19
00:00:57,934 --> 00:01:02,026
credentials injected safely through Kubernetes secrets.

20
00:01:02,026 --> 00:01:04,947
Manage it all with the Mirage CLI.

21
00:01:04,947 --> 00:01:06,960
List previews.

22
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:08,960
Grab the URL.

23
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,960
Stream logs.

24
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:13,118
Diagnose issues.

25
00:01:13,118 --> 00:01:15,157
Estimate cost.

26
00:01:15,157 --> 00:01:21,184
When the PR closes — or the TTL expires — Mirage tears everything down.

27
00:01:21,184 --> 00:01:22,644
Clean.

28
00:01:22,644 --> 00:01:24,328
Isolated.

29
00:01:24,328 --> 00:01:25,750
Gone.

30
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:27,289
Mirage.

31
00:01:27,289 --> 00:01:30,486
Appears for a PR. Vanishes when done.

